<Legal title="Terms and conditions" updated="14 October 2026">
  <h2>1. About OpenCash</h2>
  <p>OpenCash is a non-custodial interface to Perpl perpetual futures on the Monad network. It also provides bins (themed baskets of Perpl markets), rule-based bots, strategy testing tools and market data. It is available as an Android app and on the web. OpenCash is not an exchange, a broker or a bank. Trades are placed on Perpl, and funds stay in your own account.</p>
  <p>By using the app or this website you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, do not use OpenCash.</p>

  <h2>2. Early access</h2>
  <p>OpenCash is in early access. Features can change, break or be removed, and some parts may run on test networks. We do not promise that any feature will stay available.</p>

  <h2>3. Eligibility</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You must be at least 18 years old.</li>
    <li>You must not use OpenCash where trading derivatives or leveraged products is restricted or prohibited for you.</li>
    <li>You are responsible for knowing and following the laws that apply to you, including tax and reporting rules.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Self-custody and your passkey</h2>
  <p>Your account is controlled by a passkey on your device. OpenCash does not hold your funds and cannot move them for you. We do not hold a copy of your keys.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>If you lose your passkey and have no other way to sign in, you lose access to the account. We cannot recover it.</li>
    <li>If you import a private key, you are responsible for keeping it safe. Anyone who has it controls the funds.</li>
    <li>You are responsible for the security of your devices and for every action signed with your passkey.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Trading risk</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Perpetual futures are high risk. Leverage multiplies both gains and losses.</li>
    <li>Your position can be liquidated, and you can lose all of the funds you put into a position. Fast markets, thin order books and gaps can make losses larger than you expect.</li>
    <li>Prices, rankings, signals, analytics and strategy results are information, not financial, investment or tax advice.</li>
    <li>Backtests, paper trading and past results of any strategy or trader do not predict live results. Live trading has costs, slippage and failures that simulations do not show.</li>
    <li>Only trade with money you can afford to lose.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Bots and automation</h2>
  <p>Server bots trade on your behalf only under a mandate that you sign, and they use a trade-only Perpl key that cannot withdraw funds. Each bot runs within the allocation and leverage limits set for it.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>You can stop or delete a bot at any time.</li>
    <li>Automation can fail. Bots depend on our servers, Perpl, the network and market data, any of which can be slow, unavailable or wrong.</li>
    <li>We do not guarantee uptime, order fills, prices or timing.</li>
    <li>Stop orders are best effort. They may fill at a worse price than expected, or not at all.</li>
    <li>We may pause or stop all bots at any time, for example for maintenance or safety.</li>
    <li>You are responsible for checking your bots and positions and for the settings you choose.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Fees</h2>
  <p>Perpl charges its own trading fees, and the network charges gas where it applies. These fees are set by those services, not by us.</p>
  <p>Orders and bots may carry an OpenCash builder code on Perpl, which pays OpenCash a small fee set within a maximum that you approve. Swap quotes from third-party bridges may include a fee if one is configured. Any fee that applies is shown in the quote or order details, or is visible on the Perpl venue.</p>

  <h2>8. Referral codes</h2>
  <p>Referral codes are promotional. A code may raise limits such as the number of bots and the leverage a live bot can use. We can change, limit, expire or revoke a code and the benefits that come with it at any time. Do not sell, abuse or automate the use of codes.</p>

